       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. Sertraline 1000 mg daily is five times the maximum labeled dose, and you haven't given a clinical rationale. No standard indication or protocol supports it, and the risk of serious harm is high. Confirming the dose doesn't change that.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Enter a standard dose now.** Give me 50, 100, or 200 mg once daily and I'll enter it immediately.\n- **Review the dose with pharmacy or your attending.** If there is a specific reason for the higher dose, they can help document it and put it through the right channels. Poison control (1-800-222-1222 in the US) can also advise.\n- **Check for a transcription error.** If this came from a handoff note or a verbal order, it may have been meant as 100 mg.\n\nIf the situation is something else, such as a suspected ingestion or overdose, that needs urgent clinical management rather than a medication order. Tell me what's going on and I'll help with whatever order is appropriate."
      }
